#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.9"
# dependencies = ["pyyaml"]
# ///
"""tools/drift-check — prove the pool still matches its sources, and say how not.

The pre-cutover invariant (PLAN.md M2): every pool lecture equals its CANONICAL
mirror copy modulo the rewrites recorded in ``sync/ledger.yml``. The ledger
also records, as of promotion, the digest of every other series' copy of the
same lecture. This script compares all of that against the reconstructed
``mirror/`` and sorts what it finds into four outcomes:

* ``refresh`` — the canonical copy moved upstream. The pool copy is stale, not
  wrong: ``tools/promote --refresh`` re-copies it. CI does this automatically
  and opens a pull request.
* ``drift``   — a NON-canonical copy (today: the dp copy of an advanced or
  intermediate lecture) no longer matches its canonical home, or a copy was
  removed upstream, or a watched ``_toc.yml`` changed. Each becomes a GitHub
  issue (``--issues``) that closes itself when the finding clears.
* ``violation`` — the POOL itself no longer equals rewrites(canonical), or a
  pool asset changed: someone edited the pool directly, which the upstream-
  first rule forbids. Exit code 2; a red run is the alarm.
* ``info``    — nothing to act on now, but worth reading: a non-canonical copy
  that is merely stale (canonical moved, the copy did not), an ``interim``
  entry whose divergent copy moved again, or a divergence that converged.

Usage
-----
    tools/drift-check                      # report against the existing mirror/
    tools/drift-check --reconstruct        # rebuild mirror/ for the series the
                                           # ledger references, then report
    tools/drift-check --json PATH          # also write a machine-readable report
    tools/drift-check --issues             # open/update/close `drift` issues
                                           # on GitHub (needs `gh`, authenticated)
    tools/drift-check --accept-toc SERIES  # record SERIES' _toc.yml at its
                                           # current pin as the watched baseline

Exit status: 0 clean (info only), 1 drift or refresh findings, 2 violations or
an error. The script never writes to the pool or the mirror. The only
repository file it writes is ``sync/toc.yml``, under ``--accept-toc``;
``--json PATH`` writes the report wherever PATH points, and under GitHub
Actions it appends step outputs to ``$GITHUB_OUTPUT``. ``--issues`` writes to
GitHub, not to the checkout.

The toc watch: a series' ``_toc.yml`` is watched once it has been accepted
(``sync/toc.yml`` records the digest and the pin it was taken at). Accept a
series when a product manifest is generated from its toc; until then a toc
change is upstream's business, not the pool's.
"""

